<title>HUNGARY: SOCCER-ROSENBORG SNATCH LATE WINNER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-ROSENBORG SNATCH LATE WINNER.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>A goal two minutes from time by Sigurd Rushfeldt gave Rosenborg Trondheim of Norway a 1-0 win over MTK Budapest in their replayed European Cup preliminary round first leg match on Thursday.</p>
<p>Rushfeldt headed in a corner from Runar Berg.</p>
<p>Rosenborg had had a goal disallowed in the 70th minute when the impressive Mini Jakobsen was adjudged to have handled before he shot past MTK goalkeeper Gabor Babos.</p>
<p>Rushfeldt's goal was a bitter blow for MTK who had led 3-2 on Wednesday when the game was abandoned midway through the second half following a floodlight failure.</p>
</text>
